# Subscribe

---

If you want to keep up with any changes on this site, but don't feel like
checking it often, you can subscribe to any of the feeds listed below. Raw
feeds aren't for human consumption -- you'll need to copy these links into an
RSS / Atom reader.

- [*`Atom feed`*][]: The preferred method using the superior Atom format
- [*`RSS feed`*][]: For readers that don't support Atom
- [*`JSON feed`*][]: For readers that support [JSON feeds][]

[*`Atom feed`*]: /feed/atom.xml
[*`RSS feed`*]: /feed/rss.xml
[*`JSON feed`*]: /feed/feed.json
[JSON feeds]: https://www.jsonfeed.org

## RSS / Atom Readers

---

[RSS][] (Really Simple Syndication) and [Atom][] (Atom Syndication Format)
feeds offer another way to get content from this website. Subscribing to RSS /
Atom feeds allows you to keep track of multiple websites in a single feed
reader program (desktop, app, browser extension), which monitors sites for new
content, removing the need for the user to manually do so.

[RSS]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RSS
[Atom]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atom_(web_standard)

::: tabset

# Windows

Other than my servers, I run windows on all my computers, so these are the
programs I'd use.

- [RSSOwl][]: This is what I personally use, but it's a bit outdated. 
- [Raven Reader][]: Great UI, open source, and available on linux too. I'd
upgrade to this if I ever got a new computer.
- [Fluent Reader][]: A more modern RSS reader. Can be run locally or self-hosted.

[RSSOwl]: https://github.com/Xyrio/RSSOwlnix
[Raven Reader]: https://ravenreader.app
[Fluent Reader]: https://hyliu.me/fluent-reader

# Apple Mac / IOS

I don't use any Apple devices other than an Apple TV and an iPad for
ForeFlight. So while I can't personally recommend anything, I've heard good
things about these.

- [NetNewsWire][]: Incredibly polished, fast, and open source. You can also
sync via iCloud.
- [Reeder][]: Pretty flexible, and makes processing a lot of feeds easy.

[NetNewsWire]: https://netnewswire.com
[Reeder]: https://reederapp.com

# Linux

I don't run any Linux computers with a GUI, but these seem like decent choices.

- [Mozilla Thunderbird][]: I use this as an email client too and it does the
job.
- [Raven Reader][]: Great UI, open source, and available on Windows too.
- [Newsboat][]: RSS/Atom in the terminal

[Mozilla Thunderbird]: https://www.thunderbird.net
[Raven Reader]: https://ravenreader.app
[Newsboat]: https://github.com/newsboat/newsboat

:::
